// wadsum.momo - `wadinfo /s`, the summary, as a fixture of its own (DESIGN §41).
//
// The program is `wadinfo`'s, from `shared/lib/moinfo.momo`, and only the
// command tail differs: a project has one `.args`, so a mode wants a project.
// The switch comes first and in capitals, which the tail has to accept.
//
// `BASE.WAD` and `PATCH.WAD` are copies of `wadinfo`'s, byte for byte - a
// change is made there and copied here. `DUPS.WAD` is this project's own,
// built from the manifest in `fixture/` by the command at its top, and loaded
// third: it holds a name twice in one file, which the summary counts, two
// names earlier files already carry, which it prints however much it counts,
// and four alias sets, of which it names the largest three. PATCH.WAD's damage
// prints in full here as it does under no switch, and its alias set does not.

include "lib/moinfo.momo"

infoRun()
